WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.026 --> 00:00:02.931
[Applauding]
[Man]
And the only thing wrong-

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.301
The only thing wrong
with the American dream...

3
00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.969
is people-
too many people-

4
00:00:08.046 --> 00:00:12.250
too many of us telling young people
that the dream is dead.

5
00:00:12.323 --> 00:00:15.160
They told me that
when I was growing up
in the slums ofTrenton.

6
00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.463
[Audience Grumbling]
And they were wrong.

7
00:00:17.535 --> 00:00:22.536
They told me that
when I decided to run for senator,
with only $58 in my savings account.

8
00:00:22.615 --> 00:00:25.178
And they were wrong.

9
00:00:25.254 --> 00:00:29.093
And they are still telling me that now-
that I don't have a chance because I'm black,

10
00:00:29.163 --> 00:00:34.631
because I don't have the right nose,
because I still only have $58
in my savings account.

11
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.945
[Laughing]

12
00:00:44.099 --> 00:00:48.872
With your help,
we can keep that dream alive.

13
00:00:52.053 --> 00:00:54.148
And in closing,

14
00:01:02.511 --> 00:01:04.880
just...

15
00:01:07.356 --> 00:01:09.292
let me say-

16
00:01:09.361 --> 00:01:13.029
Let me say that you should all
donate the legal maximum...

17
00:01:13.104 --> 00:01:17.045
to the next president
of the United States.

18
00:01:19.886 --> 00:01:23.987
Are you okay? Do you need
some water or something?
No. I'm fine. I'm fine, really.

19
00:01:27.238 --> 00:01:30.109
Handsome guy like you,
I bet you get 70% of the women.

20
00:01:30.178 --> 00:01:31.977
Well, here's hoping.

21
00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:34.851
Of course, it helps
your wife died of cancer.

22
00:01:34.923 --> 00:01:37.794
I mean, I'm sorry,
but the sympathy vote's
in your pocket.

23
00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:39.696
Yeah, I appreciate your support.

24
00:01:39.768 --> 00:01:44.143
[Echoing]
Listen, Senator, my union
has a hell of a war chest.

25
00:01:45.782 --> 00:01:49.085
Um, I've always been strong
on the union.

26
00:01:49.157 --> 00:01:52.562
The thing is, you always go on
in your speeches about the workers...

27
00:01:52.632 --> 00:01:55.229
in Indonesia, Cambodia, Timbuktu.

28
00:01:55.306 --> 00:01:58.336
Because I think we have a-
a moral-

29
00:01:58.413 --> 00:02:00.178
My union members are hurting.

30
00:02:00.251 --> 00:02:04.489
They don't care about
moral this and moral that.
Are you all right?

31
00:02:04.561 --> 00:02:06.224
- Senator?
- Ugh. Hey!

32
00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:08.030
The guys are gonna love that.

33
00:02:10.676 --> 00:02:14.674
[Man]
Everyone, give him some room.
Give him room to breathe!

34
00:02:14.753 --> 00:02:18.660
Back off, please!
Senator, are you all right?

35
00:02:52.511 --> 00:02:55.609
[Vogler]
The senator's suffering from nausea,
headache and mental confusion.

36
00:02:55.685 --> 00:02:58.681
Ah, bad sushi
is so hard to diagnose.

37
00:03:00.798 --> 00:03:03.292
You're being childish.

38
00:03:03.371 --> 00:03:07.005
Look, ifhis case is as trivial
as you think, it'll take you
three minutes to diagnose.

39
00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:11.021
Uh-huh. Three minutes that I
could spend sitting on the toilet
with the funny pages.

40
00:03:12.126 --> 00:03:14.757
- You're mad at me.
- Nope.

41
00:03:14.832 --> 00:03:17.565
I never liked Cameron or Foreman.

42
00:03:17.639 --> 00:03:21.979
You know why I'm forcing you
to fire one of them? Because you need
to prove to me that you're a team player.

43
00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:25.046
Now, if you did that,
you wouldn't need to go
through this exercise.

44
00:03:25.123 --> 00:03:29.566
Fine. I'll hold the senator's hair
while he upchucks.

45
00:03:29.635 --> 00:03:31.902
Oh, and, uh, by the way,

46
00:03:31.973 --> 00:03:35.505
I need you to give a speech
at the National Cardiology Conference,
um, next week.

47
00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.609
I don't do speeches. I'm shy.

48
00:03:37.687 --> 00:03:41.993
Eastbrook Pharmaceuticals
has developed a new ACE inhibitor.

49
00:03:42.065 --> 00:03:46.063
I would like you to extol the virtues
of this breakthrough medication.

50
00:03:46.141 --> 00:03:48.305
Eastbrook Pharmaceuticals?

51
00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.681
Wait a second?
Don't I own that company?

52
00:03:50.753 --> 00:03:52.746
Oh, no, that's right. You do.

53
00:03:52.824 --> 00:03:56.993
Viopril is a significant improvement
over the old version.

54
00:03:57.068 --> 00:03:59.095
It's all there in the study.

55
00:03:59.173 --> 00:04:01.303
I know its price tag
is significantly improved.

56
00:04:01.378 --> 00:04:05.912
[Sighs]
You can either give one 10-minute talk
and one three-minute diagnosis,

57
00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:08.929
or you can fire one of your pets.

58
00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:15.341
My understanding was that you believed
in rationality above all else.

59
00:04:22.697 --> 00:04:24.827
Viopril.

60
00:04:25.904 --> 00:04:28.535
[Senator]
I appreciate your keeping
the media away.

61
00:04:28.611 --> 00:04:32.211
We're keeping
your staff away as well.
Take it easy now.

62
00:04:32.286 --> 00:04:35.691
- I'm in the middle of a campaign.
- The faster we can get you better,
the faster you can get out of here.

63
00:04:35.761 --> 00:04:39.098
Anyone else
at the fund-raiser get sick?

64
00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.632
I don't think so, and I don't think that's it.
I've been under the weather for weeks.

65
00:04:42.712 --> 00:04:46.174
Lots of traveling. I'm supposed
to be in the Sudan next week.

66
00:04:46.254 --> 00:04:48.851
- [Electronic Beeping]
- Oh!

67
00:04:49.762 --> 00:04:51.926
Helps me concentrate.

68
00:04:52.001 --> 00:04:54.700
- [Bottle Lid Pops]
- Even better than drugs.

69
00:04:55.677 --> 00:04:57.841
Open your mouth, please.

70
00:04:59.519 --> 00:05:02.150
Ahh.

71
00:05:02.226 --> 00:05:04.162
That's quite a scar.

72
00:05:04.231 --> 00:05:06.964
When I was six, I fell off the swing
and bit my tongue.

73
00:05:07.038 --> 00:05:09.943
Couldn't talk right
for the longest time.
[Chuckling]

74
00:05:10.011 --> 00:05:14.818
Lots of teasing.
It just made me fight harder,
speak up for those who can't.

75
00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:17.088
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

76
00:05:17.162 --> 00:05:22.197
Tongues heal too fast.
Your political consultants
have written you a nice story.

77
00:05:22.275 --> 00:05:26.479
In a tight race, the lispers alone
could put you over the top.

78
00:05:26.552 --> 00:05:29.149
You a Republican,
or you just hate all politicians?

79
00:05:29.225 --> 00:05:33.326
I just find being forced
to sit through drivel annoying.

80
00:05:33.402 --> 00:05:35.133
You find sincerity annoying?

81
00:05:35.206 --> 00:05:37.301
You're a black kid from the ghetto...

82
00:05:37.378 --> 00:05:40.715
who made it to Yale Law
and the United States Senate.

83
00:05:40.786 --> 00:05:44.089
That's a sufficiently mythical story.
You don't need to lie about your tongue.

84
00:05:47.569 --> 00:05:50.371
Must've missed it.

85
00:05:54.018 --> 00:05:56.113
What's wrong?

86
00:06:02.505 --> 00:06:05.535
What is it?
It's not the food.
It's your brain.

87
00:06:05.613 --> 00:06:08.450
Get an M.R.I.
And a lumbar puncture.

88
00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.513
Cancel your travel plans.

89
00:06:19.346 --> 00:06:22.649
The senator's L.P.
Showed no sign of infection,
and the M.R.I. Looks fairly clean.

90
00:06:22.721 --> 00:06:26.685
I guess we can tell him
he's fairly healthy and can go home.

91
00:06:26.764 --> 00:06:28.825
Well, there is something
in Broca's area,

92
00:06:28.903 --> 00:06:31.374
but it's small,
low intensity.

93
00:06:31.443 --> 00:06:35.384
Most likely
just background noise.
Care to bet your job on that?

94
00:06:35.452 --> 00:06:38.049
What was that?
What was what?

95
00:06:38.125 --> 00:06:41.223
You got annoyed.
That was clearly
an annoyed face.

96
00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.464
I get annoyed by glib remarks
about our futures.

97
00:06:43.539 --> 00:06:48.380
Last week you didn't get annoyed.
You made poopie in your pants.
It's weird.

98
00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:51.890
It's almost like now you know
you have nothing to worry about.

99
00:06:51.959 --> 00:06:53.952
Chase has nothing
to worry about?

100
00:06:54.031 --> 00:06:56.525
None of you has anything
to worry about.

101
00:06:56.603 --> 00:06:58.539
What happened?

102
00:06:58.608 --> 00:07:02.515
Vogler saw the error of his ways
and repented.

103
00:07:02.585 --> 00:07:06.287
The lesion could be nothing.
Also could be a brain tumor
or an infection.

104
00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.387
There's only one way
to find out which.

105
00:07:08.465 --> 00:07:11.062
You want to cut into his brain?

106
00:07:11.138 --> 00:07:14.874
Dangerous, I know.
Especially since he's a politician,
his brain's all twisted.

107
00:07:14.948 --> 00:07:19.755
But I weighed that against the risk
of him stroking out before lunch.
Call Surgery. Get it scheduled.

108
00:07:29.383 --> 00:07:33.621
- You're not pregnant.
- Well, I told you that.

109
00:07:33.693 --> 00:07:36.757
There's got to be some other reason
I'm still spotting.

110
00:07:36.834 --> 00:07:39.271
Sure. You were pregnant.

111
00:07:39.341 --> 00:07:42.542
Based on your hormone levels,
you've had a miscarriage.

112
00:07:42.615 --> 00:07:44.517
I haven't even been on a date.

113
00:07:44.586 --> 00:07:48.790
Right. And since
it's physically impossible to have sex
without someone buying you dinner-

114
00:07:48.863 --> 00:07:52.668
I haven't had sex
since I split up with my husband.

115
00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:56.374
- That was almost a year ago.
- Fine. Have it your way.

116
00:07:56.449 --> 00:07:58.385
Immaculate conception.

117
00:07:58.454 --> 00:08:02.658
- Um, what do I do?
- Well, it's obvious.

118
00:08:03.766 --> 00:08:05.702
Start a religion.

119
00:08:08.678 --> 00:08:10.671
In my office.

120
00:08:14.593 --> 00:08:17.430
Afternoon delight.
She just loves the hard wood.

121
00:08:19.538 --> 00:08:23.536
You're not doing a brain biopsy
based on a spot on an M.R.I.

122
00:08:23.615 --> 00:08:25.551
[Throws File Down]
Where'd you get that?

123
00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:27.715
Not on a United States senator.

124
00:08:27.792 --> 00:08:31.961
Oh, just so I'm clear-
If he was a janitor, that would be okay?
Do you have a list?

125
00:08:32.035 --> 00:08:35.304
A brain biopsy can cause
permanent neurological damage.

126
00:08:35.377 --> 00:08:38.977
Uh-huh. Whereas tumors
are really good for brains.
Make 'em grow big and strong.

127
00:08:39.052 --> 00:08:42.253
- It's my call.
- No, it's not.

128
00:08:42.327 --> 00:08:45.961
- You're pulling rank on patient care?
- It's not my call either.

129
00:08:46.036 --> 00:08:50.980
- It's up to you.
- Either it's a tumor or it's an infection
that the lumbar puncture didn't pick up.

130
00:08:51.048 --> 00:08:53.542
Either way,
unless we treat it immediately,
it could kill you.

131
00:08:53.621 --> 00:08:56.184
Or it could be nothing.
Reading brain M.R.I.'s
is not an exact science.

132
00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.287
Well, what caused my s-symptoms?

133
00:08:58.365 --> 00:09:01.236
Wow! Excellent question.
Many doctors wouldn't
have gone there.

134
00:09:01.306 --> 00:09:03.367
It could be
a transient ischemic attack.

135
00:09:03.445 --> 00:09:08.047
You could make the argument
for watching carefully
for the time being.

136
00:09:08.122 --> 00:09:11.654
Hmm, but you'd only make that argument
if you were an administrator
covering your ass.

137
00:09:11.732 --> 00:09:14.260
That's absurd and insulting.
Insulting, yes.

138
00:09:14.337 --> 00:09:16.398
What would the voters think?

139
00:09:16.476 --> 00:09:20.680
If they find out
I've had a b-brain biopsy?

140
00:09:22.558 --> 00:09:25.554
This could leave you
b-b-b-brain damaged,

141
00:09:25.631 --> 00:09:27.932
and you're worried
about NASCAR dads?

142
00:09:30.176 --> 00:09:32.237
[Whirring]

143
00:09:46.382 --> 00:09:48.249
It's not a brain tumor.

144
00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.518
It's not a bacterial infection either.

145
00:09:50.592 --> 00:09:53.793
So you biopsied his brain
for nothing?

146
00:09:53.867 --> 00:09:58.606
If that were true,
would Dr. Wilson's mouth
be contorted into that ugly shape?

147
00:10:00.683 --> 00:10:03.052
It's toxoplasmosis.

148
00:10:03.123 --> 00:10:05.116
You sure?

149
00:10:05.194 --> 00:10:08.634
Which means the Great Black Hope
has full-blown Al DS.

150
00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.078
They're gonna love that
in Dubuque.

151
00:10:18.025 --> 00:10:21.430
Toxoplasmosis
is a fairly common fungus
you can get...

152
00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:24.632
from eating under-cooked meat
or touching cat feces.

153
00:10:24.709 --> 00:10:27.978
In rare cases,
the fungi travel up the bloodstream
and latch onto the brain,

154
00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:30.955
causing a lesion
or inflammation.

155
00:10:31.024 --> 00:10:33.518
So, what's the prognosis?

156
00:10:36.404 --> 00:10:39.103
Toxo usually responds
to treatment,

157
00:10:39.177 --> 00:10:43.552
but it only causes a lesion in your brain
if your immune system is extremely weak
to begin with.

158
00:10:46.628 --> 00:10:48.826
Senator, I'm afraid you have Al DS.

159
00:10:52.142 --> 00:10:54.670
- [Scoffs]
- As I'm sure-

160
00:10:54.748 --> 00:10:58.655
No!
As I'm sure you know,
people with H.I.V. Can live a long time.

161
00:10:58.724 --> 00:11:02.426
- What else could do this to me?
- Theoretically, certain cancers.

162
00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:05.439
If you have toxo in your brain,
you have AIDS.

163
00:11:06.844 --> 00:11:10.615
I do not have Al DS.

164
00:11:10.687 --> 00:11:14.355
I don't sh- sh- shoot up drugs.

165
00:11:14.429 --> 00:11:18.165
I don't s-sleep with-

166
00:11:18.238 --> 00:11:21.234
This is very bad news.
I get that, and I sympathize.

167
00:11:21.313 --> 00:11:25.585
But we gotta speed through
the denial phase because you need
antiretrovirals and you need them fast.

168
00:11:28.998 --> 00:11:33.133
But-You haven't even
tested me for H.I.V.!

169
00:11:33.208 --> 00:11:37.149
- We will.
- But the toxo drugs
are gonna piss off your fungi.

170
00:11:37.217 --> 00:11:39.278
And when fungi get pissed-

171
00:11:39.356 --> 00:11:42.956
- [Clattering]
- I am not going to take the pills.

172
00:11:43.032 --> 00:11:45.663
You're afraid word will leak out.

173
00:11:47.442 --> 00:11:49.913
Trust me. You're not gonna
be president either way.

174
00:11:49.982 --> 00:11:52.887
They don't call it the White House
because of the paint job.

175
00:11:52.956 --> 00:11:55.325
Here's what you're gonna do.

176
00:11:55.395 --> 00:11:59.496
You're gonna give me the drugs
for the toxo only.

177
00:12:00.775 --> 00:12:04.078
You're going to test me for H.I.V.,
under a false name.

178
00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:06.815
You are going to test me for cancer...

179
00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.886
and anything else
that could have done this to me.

180
00:12:09.964 --> 00:12:13.496
If I have cancer,
I will deal with it.

181
00:12:16.245 --> 00:12:18.773
But I do not...

182
00:12:18.852 --> 00:12:21.415
have Al DS.

183
00:12:23.797 --> 00:12:26.291
"Eastbrook Pharmaceuticals
are pleased to announce...

184
00:12:26.371 --> 00:12:31.007
that Dr. Gregory House
will present the latest research
on our exciting new ACE inhibitor."

185
00:12:32.018 --> 00:12:35.082
[Scoffs]
You're making that up.
That's Vogler's company.

186
00:12:35.158 --> 00:12:39.726
Press release.
"During an address at the North
American Cardiology Conference."

187
00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:46.615
- House never gives speeches.
- But when I really believe in something-

188
00:12:46.686 --> 00:12:49.523
Gosh dang it, I got a chance
to make a difference here.

189
00:12:49.593 --> 00:12:51.529
You made a deal with Vogler?

190
00:12:52.767 --> 00:12:55.261
It's all the rage.
Everybody's doing it.

191
00:12:56.377 --> 00:13:01.150
So, what's the deal?
You get to keep all of us
if you flog his products?

192
00:13:01.221 --> 00:13:03.020
One speech. No biggie.

193
00:13:03.093 --> 00:13:07.559
Foreman's doing a bone marrow biopsy
to check for cancer.

194
00:13:07.637 --> 00:13:09.368
Cancer?
The senator's got Al DS.

195
00:13:09.441 --> 00:13:11.878
Cancer sounds better
in a press release.

196
00:13:11.948 --> 00:13:14.750
I need you guys to rush
the ELISA test for H.I.V.

197
00:13:14.821 --> 00:13:16.985
Thank you.

198
00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:18.825
For the speech.

199
00:13:18.898 --> 00:13:21.392
When I said rush,
I meant, you know, fast.

200
00:13:21.470 --> 00:13:24.443
- "Stat's" the word you doctors use, right?
- I know it's hard for you.

201
00:13:24.512 --> 00:13:26.448
Double stat?

202
00:13:29.757 --> 00:13:32.753
[Moans Quietly]
This may sting a little.

203
00:13:33.867 --> 00:13:37.329
Sorry.
[Coughs]
It wasn't the shot.

204
00:13:37.409 --> 00:13:41.043
It's, um- My head's killing me.

205
00:13:41.118 --> 00:13:43.783
Senator, we don't have
to do this now.

206
00:13:43.858 --> 00:13:47.195
We can hold off
till your H.I.V. Test comes back.
[Laughing]

207
00:13:47.266 --> 00:13:49.965
Because you figure
it's gonna come back positive.

208
00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:52.135
In my experience-
Patients lie.

209
00:13:52.212 --> 00:13:56.153
Politicians lie more.
Black politicians-

210
00:13:56.222 --> 00:13:59.161
Oh. I don't think black politicians lie
more than white politicians.

211
00:13:59.229 --> 00:14:03.034
- We lie less.
- You figure we're morally superior?

212
00:14:03.105 --> 00:14:06.135
[Chuckling]
I've got my theories.

213
00:14:06.212 --> 00:14:10.381
No, we-
we just can't get away with it.

214
00:14:10.456 --> 00:14:12.392
[Clears Throat]

215
00:14:12.461 --> 00:14:16.904
No one's gonna g-give us
the benefit of the doubt.

216
00:14:16.972 --> 00:14:19.671
No one's gonna cut us
a second chance.

217
00:14:19.746 --> 00:14:24.155
And when it happens,
it's not just a- a bad politician.

218
00:14:24.223 --> 00:14:26.524
It's- It's a bad role model.

219
00:14:26.595 --> 00:14:30.057
It's a- a dis-

220
00:14:30.138 --> 00:14:33.874
discredit to the race.

221
00:14:44.505 --> 00:14:47.410
You ready?
Yeah.

222
00:14:48.515 --> 00:14:50.451
Yeah.

223
00:14:51.689 --> 00:14:55.630
Take a deep breath.
[Grunts]

224
00:14:56.701 --> 00:14:58.899
[Gasping]

225
00:15:03.051 --> 00:15:06.183
Dr. House, I just wanted-

226
00:15:06.258 --> 00:15:08.593
You're welcome again.
I want you to know how much-

227
00:15:08.664 --> 00:15:11.192
Got it. You're grateful.

228
00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:14.107
Apparently you seem to think
it will mean a lot to me to know that.

229
00:15:14.177 --> 00:15:16.671
Do you know why people
pray to God?

230
00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:19.221
I thought
you didn't believe in God.
I don't.

231
00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:21.693
Well, then you better be making
a very good point.

232
00:15:21.762 --> 00:15:25.224
Do you think they pray to him
and praise him because they want him
to know how great he is?

233
00:15:25.304 --> 00:15:26.864
God already knows that.

234
00:15:28.546 --> 00:15:31.211
Are you comparing me to God?

235
00:15:31.286 --> 00:15:33.883
I mean, that's great,
but just so you know,
I've never made a tree.

236
00:15:36.164 --> 00:15:39.194
I thank you because
it means something to me...

237
00:15:40.775 --> 00:15:42.768
to be grateful
for what I receive.

238
00:15:49.195 --> 00:15:51.792
You are the most naive atheist
I've ever met.

239
00:15:51.869 --> 00:15:54.774
Dr. House, you have
a patient in room one.

240
00:15:54.843 --> 00:15:58.146
Thank God.

241
00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:02.752
People pray so that God
won't crush them like bugs.

242
00:16:06.604 --> 00:16:09.075
I'm not gonna crush you.

243
00:16:12.686 --> 00:16:15.682
"Petechial" bruising?
I don't know if I pronounced that right.

244
00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:18.425
Gosh, the Internet
is such a wonderful tool.

245
00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:22.100
It could be leukemia.
Definitely possible.

246
00:16:22.176 --> 00:16:24.511
The more likely diagnosis
is hickey.

247
00:16:24.582 --> 00:16:27.315
Well, it can't be a hickey.

248
00:16:27.388 --> 00:16:29.882
Why is everybody so ashamed of sex
all of a sudden?

249
00:16:29.962 --> 00:16:31.864
I'm not having sex.

250
00:16:31.933 --> 00:16:35.236
I've barely even thought about sex
since my marriage. Ow!

251
00:16:35.307 --> 00:16:37.972
I say you're having sex,
you say you're not.

252
00:16:38.047 --> 00:16:40.986
Either you're lying
or I'm wrong.

253
00:16:41.055 --> 00:16:44.187
- Or there's some middle ground.
- You mean, like, oral?

254
00:16:44.262 --> 00:16:46.733
I mean, you're having sex
without knowing it.

255
00:16:46.802 --> 00:16:49.866
I'm testing you for booze,
drugs and G.H.B.

256
00:16:49.943 --> 00:16:53.348
I don't drink or-What's G.H.B.?

257
00:16:53.418 --> 00:16:55.582
The date-rape drug.

258
00:17:12.965 --> 00:17:14.901
It's positive.

259
00:17:28.838 --> 00:17:31.207
Your "T" cell count is eight,

260
00:17:31.276 --> 00:17:33.770
which means
there's a good chance you'll die.

261
00:17:35.453 --> 00:17:39.485
I'm telling you this because we need
to contact your sexual partners.

262
00:17:39.563 --> 00:17:42.330
I've only had two girlfriends.

263
00:17:42.403 --> 00:17:45.535
Two. After my wife died.

264
00:17:45.612 --> 00:17:49.074
I used c-condoms.

265
00:17:49.154 --> 00:17:53.563
You know the chances of you getting H.I. V.
From heterosexual sex with a condom?

266
00:17:53.631 --> 00:17:55.761
Yes.

267
00:17:55.836 --> 00:17:57.772
Someday there will be
a black president.

268
00:17:57.841 --> 00:18:00.005
Someday there will be
a gay president.

269
00:18:00.079 --> 00:18:03.109
Maybe there'll even be
a gay, black president.

270
00:18:03.188 --> 00:18:06.890
But one combination
I do not see happening
is gay, black and dead.

271
00:18:08.634 --> 00:18:10.695
You need to stop lying to me.

272
00:18:10.773 --> 00:18:13.940
It must be miserable,
always assuming the worst in people.

273
00:18:14.013 --> 00:18:16.074
Cut the crap. You're dying.

274
00:18:16.152 --> 00:18:19.319
And you're clever, you're witty
and you are a coward.

275
00:18:19.393 --> 00:18:21.762
You're scared of taking chances.

276
00:18:21.833 --> 00:18:25.273
- I take chances all the time.
It's one of my worst qualities.
- On people?

277
00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:32.621
Wanting to believe
the best about people
doesn't make it true.

278
00:18:32.692 --> 00:18:34.525
Being afraid to believe it
doesn't make it false.

279
00:18:34.597 --> 00:18:37.502
Well, that's very moving.
It's a shame I don't vote.
Hmm.

280
00:18:37.571 --> 00:18:40.840
This is who I am.
I believe in people.

281
00:18:40.913 --> 00:18:44.148
I'm not hiply cynical,
and I don't make easy, snide remarks.

282
00:18:44.221 --> 00:18:48.960
I would rather think that people are good
and be disappointed once and again.

283
00:19:06.074 --> 00:19:08.238
I need to draw some more blood.

284
00:19:41.492 --> 00:19:44.590
Nurse!

285
00:19:44.667 --> 00:19:46.660
The antiretrovirals aren't working.

286
00:19:46.739 --> 00:19:48.732
That's not surprising.

287
00:19:50.047 --> 00:19:52.541
He's just gonna keep getting worse.
You realize that, right?

288
00:19:52.619 --> 00:19:54.680
Why are you spying on my case?

289
00:19:54.758 --> 00:19:56.956
Why are you giving
that speech next week?

290
00:19:57.031 --> 00:19:59.798
We're both just doing
what we have to do.
You don't see a problem with that?

291
00:19:59.871 --> 00:20:02.206
Checking in on a patient?

292
00:20:02.276 --> 00:20:04.907
Yeah, wow. How do I look
myself in the mirror?

293
00:20:04.983 --> 00:20:07.580
You're not the one being asked
to perpetrate a fraud
on the American people.

294
00:20:07.656 --> 00:20:10.652
It's a 10-minute speech.
That I've been ordered to give.

295
00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:13.327
Vogler's drug works.
Don't care.

296
00:20:13.403 --> 00:20:17.401
Why do you have to make
everything so dramatic?
I'm a very high-strung little lap dog.

297
00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:22.116
[Growls, Yipping, Growls]

298
00:20:22.192 --> 00:20:24.527
[Barks]

299
00:20:24.597 --> 00:20:26.294
[Grunting]

300
00:20:28.707 --> 00:20:31.544
Uh-uh. No pills.

301
00:20:31.614 --> 00:20:33.277
What's going on?

302
00:20:33.351 --> 00:20:36.586
The antiretrovirals
aren't working.

303
00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:39.565
Why not?

304
00:20:39.633 --> 00:20:42.070
Because you don't have Al DS.

305
00:20:44.011 --> 00:20:46.141
The first test was a false positive.

306
00:20:46.217 --> 00:20:48.654
Happens one time in every 5,000.

307
00:20:48.722 --> 00:20:51.285
You r-ran a second test?

308
00:20:51.362 --> 00:20:54.335
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

309
00:20:55.439 --> 00:20:57.375
You're still dying.

310
00:20:59.214 --> 00:21:03.554
The only difference is,
now we don't know why.

311
00:21:14.118 --> 00:21:16.817
He's continuing to lose control
of the muscles on his right side.

312
00:21:16.891 --> 00:21:21.129
- His brain is getting foggier,
and his "T" cells are still in single digits.
- Why are we doing this here?

313
00:21:21.201 --> 00:21:23.228
So Cuddy can't find us.

314
00:21:23.307 --> 00:21:27.112
Unless we figure out
the underlying disease,
this guy's lied to his last constituent.

315
00:21:27.182 --> 00:21:30.246
- False negative
on the P.C.R. Al DS test?
- Ran it twice.

316
00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.259
- Immunoglobulin deficiency?
- No history of respiratory problems.

317
00:21:34.334 --> 00:21:36.270
Idiopathic "T" cell deficiency.

318
00:21:36.338 --> 00:21:41.008
Idiopathic- from the Latin
meaning "we're idiots" 'cause we
can't figure out what's causing it.

319
00:21:41.952 --> 00:21:44.150
[Sighs]
Give him a whole body scan.

320
00:21:44.224 --> 00:21:47.220
- You hate whole body scans.
- 'Cause they're useless.

321
00:21:47.298 --> 00:21:51.239
Could probably scan any one of us
and find five different doodads
that look like cancer.

322
00:21:51.308 --> 00:21:54.804
But when you're fourth down
and a hundred to go, in the snow,

323
00:21:54.883 --> 00:21:57.822
you don't call
a running play up the middle,
unless you're theJets.

324
00:22:00.430 --> 00:22:02.491
I hate sports metaphors.

325
00:22:02.568 --> 00:22:04.835
Why did you order
the second AIDS test?

326
00:22:04.907 --> 00:22:08.039
Standard procedure.
Oh, well, that's you-
Mr. Standard Procedure.

327
00:22:08.115 --> 00:22:10.609
You suspected the first test
was a false positive?

328
00:22:10.688 --> 00:22:14.493
I knew he was going to Africa,
and I figured he was vaccinated
for Hep "A" and "B."

329
00:22:14.564 --> 00:22:16.557
That could cause a false positive.

330
00:22:16.636 --> 00:22:21.637
- You knew that before you ordered
the first test. What changed?
- I should have ordered both.

331
00:22:21.714 --> 00:22:23.707
You were sure he had Al DS.

332
00:22:23.786 --> 00:22:27.386
Then you talked to him,
then you had doubts.
What did he say?

333
00:22:27.463 --> 00:22:32.065
He said he had not engaged
in any risky behavior.

334
00:22:32.140 --> 00:22:34.133
Huh. And you believed him.

335
00:22:34.212 --> 00:22:36.479
He didn't have any reason to lie.

336
00:22:36.551 --> 00:22:39.114
Everybody lies, except politicians?

337
00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:42.858
House,
I believe you're a romantic.

338
00:22:42.933 --> 00:22:45.370
You didn't just believe him,
you believed in him!

339
00:22:45.439 --> 00:22:48.172
Do you want to come over tonight
and watch old movies and cry?

340
00:22:48.246 --> 00:22:50.979
Dr. Cameron's getting to you.

341
00:22:51.052 --> 00:22:53.819
Well, I guess you can't
be around that much niceness
and not get any on you.

342
00:22:53.893 --> 00:22:56.228
Is that why you haven't put
the moves on her?

343
00:22:56.299 --> 00:22:59.899
What makes you think
I haven't put the moves on her?

344
00:23:01.879 --> 00:23:05.182
Oh! Oh, boy! You're in trouble.

345
00:23:12.003 --> 00:23:14.440
[Door Opens]

346
00:23:15.645 --> 00:23:18.447
You have restored my faith
in the human race.

347
00:23:19.522 --> 00:23:22.859
- You're lying.
- No. I'm not lying.

348
00:23:22.930 --> 00:23:26.370
Just got your results back.
No G.H.B., no nothing.

349
00:23:26.439 --> 00:23:29.901
It means you're having sex
and you're lying about it.

350
00:23:29.981 --> 00:23:32.783
No. And I have a new symptom.

351
00:23:32.854 --> 00:23:37.058
I have a rash on my butt.
[Chuckles]

352
00:23:38.368 --> 00:23:41.968
Do you wanna? Yeah.

353
00:23:47.923 --> 00:23:51.260
- What is it?
- It's a carpet burn.

354
00:23:51.332 --> 00:23:53.427
No. It can't be.

355
00:23:53.504 --> 00:23:55.975
Doctor, I love sex.

356
00:23:56.044 --> 00:23:59.040
I miss it.
I haven't had any in over a year.

357
00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:04.620
Well, you managed to keep
this appointment, so you have
no short-term memory problem.

358
00:24:04.698 --> 00:24:08.298
Multiple personalities?
Do you find yourself
losing chunks of time?

359
00:24:08.374 --> 00:24:13.842
Do you wake up, and you don't
remember falling asleep?
No. I just wake up really exhausted.

360
00:24:13.921 --> 00:24:17.487
- Something upsetting you?
- No.

361
00:24:19.768 --> 00:24:22.673
My ex lives
in the apartment downstairs.

362
00:24:22.742 --> 00:24:26.581
He's always calling me,
always wanting to get back together,
complaining about mixed signals.

363
00:24:26.651 --> 00:24:30.422
"Get out of my life. '"
How much clearer can you get?

364
00:24:31.697 --> 00:24:34.636
We have a sleep lab
in the basement.

365
00:24:34.704 --> 00:24:38.976
If nothing else, it will get you away
from your ex for a night.

366
00:24:52.180 --> 00:24:55.347
Slightly enlarged lymph node
in his left armpit.

367
00:24:55.421 --> 00:24:57.448
How slightly?
Quarter mil.

368
00:24:57.526 --> 00:24:59.462
- Lymphoma?
- [House] Sure.

369
00:24:59.531 --> 00:25:02.094
Or he's had a cold
in the last six months.

370
00:25:02.171 --> 00:25:06.807
- What, you got her on speed dial?
- I just follow the scent of arrogance.

371
00:25:06.882 --> 00:25:11.723
Another slightly enlarged node over here.
Two more in his neck and one in his groin.

372
00:25:11.794 --> 00:25:16.032
- And there's a cyst in his liver.
- [Cameron] It looks complex.
Central necrosis?

373
00:25:16.104 --> 00:25:18.131
[House]
Spontaneous bleeding.
It's benign.

374
00:25:18.210 --> 00:25:21.742
I was rooting for a really cool tumor.
Instead we're stuck with this crap.

375
00:25:21.819 --> 00:25:24.416
Doesn't matter. Once you find 'em,
you gotta check 'em.

376
00:25:24.491 --> 00:25:28.262
Knock yourselves out.

377
00:25:28.334 --> 00:25:30.327
I just saw Senator Wright.
He looks like hell.

378
00:25:30.406 --> 00:25:33.243
That sushi must've been
a lot worse than you thought.

379
00:25:33.313 --> 00:25:37.277
Mr. Vogler, would you like
a free whole body scan?

380
00:25:37.356 --> 00:25:40.591
A man of your stature
should get himself checked
at least three times a year.

381
00:25:40.665 --> 00:25:44.800
Here's a few key points
I want you to cover
during your speech.

382
00:25:46.177 --> 00:25:48.648
[House]
Fourteen pages.

383
00:25:48.717 --> 00:25:51.484
The audience will be comatose
by paragraph two.

384
00:25:51.557 --> 00:25:53.960
Throw in a joke.

385
00:25:57.872 --> 00:26:00.571
Dr. Chase, we need to talk.

386
00:26:03.721 --> 00:26:07.092
- How do you see this ending?
- What ending?

387
00:26:07.161 --> 00:26:12.162
I can't fire you,
so you have no reason to fear me
and, therefore, no reason to lie to me.

388
00:26:12.241 --> 00:26:17.185
You told Cuddy where I was.
You told Vogler what I was doing.

389
00:26:21.630 --> 00:26:25.868
Yeah.
So how can I work with you?

390
00:26:27.077 --> 00:26:30.175
Well, you don't have a choice.

391
00:26:33.692 --> 00:26:35.925
[Foreman]
This might hurt a little.

392
00:26:35.999 --> 00:26:38.732
- Lie to me.
- [Chuckles]

393
00:26:38.806 --> 00:26:41.711
Okay.
It'll feel like a gentle massage.

394
00:26:41.779 --> 00:26:44.718
House...

395
00:26:44.786 --> 00:26:47.953
is a lousy teacher.

396
00:26:48.028 --> 00:26:51.229
You can't lie for beans.

397
00:26:51.303 --> 00:26:53.467
Have you ever told
any really big ones?

398
00:26:53.541 --> 00:26:55.477
Oh-ho-ho-ho!

399
00:26:55.546 --> 00:27:00.114
I might be messed up,
but I'm not that out of it.

400
00:27:00.190 --> 00:27:03.630
- [Grunting]
- [Foreman] Strap his arm down.

401
00:27:12.487 --> 00:27:14.958
Am I going to be okay?

402
00:27:16.029 --> 00:27:17.931
I hope so.

403
00:27:24.383 --> 00:27:26.547
I am selling my soul.

404
00:27:26.621 --> 00:27:30.289
Just a little piece.
And you are getting
something in return.

405
00:27:30.363 --> 00:27:33.302
I said I was selling it.
Didn't say I was giving it away.

406
00:27:33.371 --> 00:27:36.867
That would be immoral
and stupid.

407
00:27:36.947 --> 00:27:39.008
All they've done
is add an antacid.

408
00:27:39.085 --> 00:27:40.987
Does it work?
That's not the point.

409
00:27:41.057 --> 00:27:43.894
Of course it's the point.
He's not asking you to lie.

410
00:27:43.964 --> 00:27:47.496
He's not asking you
to do something illegal.
He's not asking me to do anything.

411
00:27:47.572 --> 00:27:50.545
He's not ordering you.
He gave you a choice.
You chose your staff.

412
00:27:52.517 --> 00:27:54.852
I know this isn't easy for you.
You'll suffer.

413
00:27:54.923 --> 00:27:57.190
Vicodin sales in Jersey will triple.

414
00:27:57.263 --> 00:27:59.290
But you are doing a good thing.

415
00:28:06.685 --> 00:28:09.783
Only you could feel like crap
about doing something good.

416
00:28:10.828 --> 00:28:14.792
Kidney and liver cysts are both benign,
and the lymph nodes all came back clean.

417
00:28:14.872 --> 00:28:19.679
- His left armpit node has antibodies for C.D. 11.
- Not enough to indicate lymphoma.

418
00:28:19.750 --> 00:28:21.845
We never tested
for hairy cell leukemia.

419
00:28:21.922 --> 00:28:25.590
No, but we would have
picked it up somewhere else
besides one lymph node.

420
00:28:25.664 --> 00:28:29.662
- And his spleen isn't enlarged.
- Size isn't everything.

421
00:28:29.741 --> 00:28:32.178
The spleen is the mother lode
for hairy cells.

422
00:28:33.684 --> 00:28:36.053
[Sighs]
Let's cut it open.

423
00:28:36.123 --> 00:28:38.526
You can't biopsy his spleen.
It'll bleed like stink.

424
00:28:38.596 --> 00:28:42.469
In the senator's condition,
a spleen biopsy could easily
cause sepsis and kill him.

425
00:28:42.538 --> 00:28:44.565
Why do you do this to me?

426
00:28:44.643 --> 00:28:48.014
Now if I kill him,
I can't tell the judge I had no idea
of the risks involved.

427
00:28:48.085 --> 00:28:51.490
His brain is turning into mush,
and he's at risk for more infections.
We have to do it.

428
00:28:51.560 --> 00:28:54.362
See? That'll sound
much better in court.

429
00:28:54.434 --> 00:28:58.375
Okay. Go tell our human pincushion
we'll be sticking him one more time.

430
00:29:00.215 --> 00:29:02.914
Cuddy.

431
00:29:02.989 --> 00:29:04.925
Don't you hate doing this?

432
00:29:06.631 --> 00:29:08.624
Yeah.

433
00:29:23.405 --> 00:29:25.398
What's up?

434
00:29:28.250 --> 00:29:30.243
You like me.

435
00:29:32.594 --> 00:29:34.530
Why?

436
00:29:37.239 --> 00:29:39.540
That's kind of a sad question.

437
00:29:42.117 --> 00:29:44.611
I'm just trying to figure out
what makes you tick.

438
00:29:44.689 --> 00:29:48.995
I am not warm and fuzzy,
and you are basically a stuffed animal
made by Grandma.

439
00:29:49.067 --> 00:29:51.060
I don't think
that's why you're asking.

440
00:29:52.609 --> 00:29:55.707
- I think this is because of the speech.
- God, don't try and pick me apart.

441
00:29:55.783 --> 00:29:57.844
Then why are you asking?

442
00:29:58.925 --> 00:30:00.861
What do you want to hear?

443
00:30:15.966 --> 00:30:20.101
[Opens Door]
[Sighs]

444
00:30:21.412 --> 00:30:25.581
Hey, Senator. We need to do
one more biopsy- on your spleen.

445
00:30:25.656 --> 00:30:29.495
[Clears Throat]
I'll have to sign lefty.

446
00:30:29.565 --> 00:30:32.059
My fingers aren't working.

447
00:30:33.675 --> 00:30:36.671
[Coughing]

448
00:30:37.952 --> 00:30:39.945
Have you been coughing a lot?

449
00:30:40.024 --> 00:30:42.085
[Gasps]
Does it hurt?

450
00:30:42.162 --> 00:30:45.101
It's like I can't get air.

451
00:30:46.406 --> 00:30:48.809
Is that from the toxo?

452
00:30:49.881 --> 00:30:53.481
No. This is-This is new.

453
00:30:55.294 --> 00:30:58.392
You don't need to sign.
We can't do the biopsy.

454
00:30:58.469 --> 00:31:02.069
[Coughing, Gasping]

455
00:31:06.521 --> 00:31:09.288
The senator's breathing
is severely impaired.

456
00:31:09.361 --> 00:31:11.662
His O2 sat levels are at 89.

457
00:31:11.735 --> 00:31:14.206
His silver stain indicates
Pneumocystis carinii pneumonia.

458
00:31:14.273 --> 00:31:17.144
Another killer fungus.
It's consistent
with hairy cell leukemia.

459
00:31:17.214 --> 00:31:20.210
[Foreman]
But we can't biopsy his spleen.
Respiratory distress.

460
00:31:20.288 --> 00:31:23.055
His platelets are 20 and dropping.
His blood won't clot worth a damn.

461
00:31:23.129 --> 00:31:25.828
[Cameron]
There's gotta be another way
to diagnose hairy cell.

462
00:31:25.902 --> 00:31:29.069
No. His bone marrow's indeterminate.
Spleen biopsy's the only way to go.

463
00:31:29.144 --> 00:31:32.117
You know, when the Inuit go fishing,
they don't look for fish.

464
00:31:39.067 --> 00:31:40.934
Why, Dr. House?

465
00:31:41.005 --> 00:31:45.345
They look for the blue heron
because there's no way to see the fish.

466
00:31:45.416 --> 00:31:48.115
But if there's fish,
there's gonna be birds fishing.

467
00:31:48.190 --> 00:31:51.425
Now, if he's got hairy cell,
what else should we see circling overhead?

468
00:31:51.497 --> 00:31:55.632
- He should have all sorts of weird viruses.
- H.T.L.V. And A.T.L.V.

469
00:31:55.707 --> 00:31:59.409
We can test for them.
Run the titers.

470
00:32:00.887 --> 00:32:03.860
These were your brain waves
at 2:45 a.m.

471
00:32:03.927 --> 00:32:07.493
Now, here it comes.
There's an abruptjump
from slow-wave sleep.

472
00:32:08.873 --> 00:32:11.470
This indicates
partial sleep arousal.

473
00:32:11.546 --> 00:32:14.781
Most common type is somnambulism.
Sleepwalking.

474
00:32:14.854 --> 00:32:17.451
That would explain why
I'm so tired when I wake up.

475
00:32:17.527 --> 00:32:19.828
Yes. And also why
you were pregnant.

476
00:32:21.303 --> 00:32:23.831
And the hickeys.
And the carpet burn.

477
00:32:23.910 --> 00:32:26.677
I had sex in my sleep?

478
00:32:26.750 --> 00:32:29.415
Sexsomnia
is a documented disorder.

479
00:32:30.993 --> 00:32:33.191
You said your ex lives downstairs.
I'll kill him.

480
00:32:33.265 --> 00:32:37.070
Okay. But he probably didn't know
that you were asleep.

481
00:32:37.142 --> 00:32:39.511
Sexsomniacs
can act pretty normal.

482
00:32:39.580 --> 00:32:42.951
I'm gonna write you a prescription
for a low-dose antidepressant.

483
00:32:43.022 --> 00:32:45.015
It'll let you sleep better.

484
00:32:45.094 --> 00:32:49.092
If you wanna save yourself the $15 co-pay,
you could have sex while you're awake.

485
00:32:50.474 --> 00:32:52.968
- He's my ex. I don't-
- You live in the same building.

486
00:32:53.046 --> 00:32:57.078
You haven't had sex
with anyone else for a year.
You sleepwalk right into his arms.

487
00:32:57.156 --> 00:33:00.254
Call me crazy,
but I'm sensing unresolved issues.

488
00:33:04.708 --> 00:33:06.872
Negative
for H.T.L.V. 1 and 2.

489
00:33:06.947 --> 00:33:09.612
And negative for A.T.L.V.
And everything else.

490
00:33:09.687 --> 00:33:12.420
It's not hairy cell.

491
00:33:12.494 --> 00:33:15.331
Hey. You really
gonna give that speech?

492
00:33:16.470 --> 00:33:19.807
You got an opinion too?
I'm a little surprised.

493
00:33:19.879 --> 00:33:23.980
Frankly, I thought you were too much
of a self-absorbed ass to do this for us.

494
00:33:24.056 --> 00:33:27.393
You're welcome.
He's positive for Epstein-Barr.

495
00:33:27.464 --> 00:33:29.457
So what?

496
00:33:29.536 --> 00:33:32.303
It doesn't point to hairy cell.
It's irrelevant.

497
00:33:42.935 --> 00:33:46.375
[Gasping]
Hey.

498
00:33:46.443 --> 00:33:48.914
You didn't fall off the swings
when you were eight.

499
00:33:48.982 --> 00:33:52.046
[Gasping Continues]
S-S-Six.

500
00:33:52.124 --> 00:33:54.527
Ever.

501
00:33:54.596 --> 00:33:57.865
Give that back.
Uh-uh. We have to talk.

502
00:33:57.937 --> 00:33:59.930
You had an epileptic seizure.

503
00:34:00.009 --> 00:34:02.173
That's how you bit your tongue.

504
00:34:02.248 --> 00:34:05.483
L-I haven't had a seizure since-

505
00:34:05.556 --> 00:34:08.927
What medication did you take?

506
00:34:08.998 --> 00:34:12.096
No s-s-seizure since I was six.

507
00:34:12.172 --> 00:34:16.774
No dr-dr-drugs s-since I was 10.

508
00:34:16.850 --> 00:34:19.948
Yeah, that's it. Don't worry about
what the question is.

509
00:34:20.025 --> 00:34:24.263
Don't worry that you're
starting to feel dizzy.
Just stay on message.

510
00:34:24.335 --> 00:34:28.140
[Gasping]

511
00:34:28.211 --> 00:34:30.272
My-
[Sobbing]

512
00:34:30.349 --> 00:34:34.655
My mother used to call it-
[Gasping]

513
00:34:34.727 --> 00:34:36.663
"Funny-something."

514
00:34:36.732 --> 00:34:39.226
- Phenytoin?
- Yes!

515
00:34:42.379 --> 00:34:44.372
Okay, okay. You're okay.

516
00:34:46.121 --> 00:34:49.117
It's okay.
[Whimpering]

517
00:34:51.434 --> 00:34:53.427
Everybody lies.

518
00:34:54.842 --> 00:35:00.116
[House]
Senator Gary H. Wright of NewJersey
had childhood epilepsy.

519
00:35:00.188 --> 00:35:02.124
He took phenytoin.

520
00:35:02.193 --> 00:35:04.186
That drug,
with the Epstein-Barr virus,

521
00:35:04.265 --> 00:35:07.295
is associated with common variable
immunodeficiency disease.

522
00:35:07.372 --> 00:35:11.576
"T" cells down, "B" cells down.
Keeps you from forming
enough antibodies.

523
00:35:11.649 --> 00:35:14.416
See, the antibodies are basically
your defensive line.

524
00:35:14.489 --> 00:35:18.294
And your brain
is like the quarterback.

525
00:35:18.366 --> 00:35:22.741
And then the fungi
are like blitzing linebackers
plunging up the middle.

526
00:35:22.810 --> 00:35:24.746
Your lungs are like-

527
00:35:26.385 --> 00:35:28.446
Okay, you got two quarterbacks.
[Chase]
C. V.I.D.?

528
00:35:28.524 --> 00:35:31.497
That's a type
of immunoglobulin deficiency.
I said that.

529
00:35:31.565 --> 00:35:35.472
Yeah. Well, it was a stupid idea
when you said it.

530
00:35:35.541 --> 00:35:38.446
Then he got the respiratory problem,
and he tested positive for Epstein-Barr.

531
00:35:38.515 --> 00:35:40.348
That's pretty much
a childhood disease.

532
00:35:40.420 --> 00:35:44.054
That's another reason why
Chase's suggestion was idiotic.
He got it when he was a kid.

533
00:35:44.129 --> 00:35:46.623
He didn't get
any symptoms until now.
It happens.

534
00:35:46.702 --> 00:35:50.575
It gets triggered by stress-
like public speaking.

535
00:35:50.644 --> 00:35:55.748
So you're basing your diagnosis
on a virus that's relatively common
and a drug he took 30 years ago.

536
00:35:55.824 --> 00:35:59.025
Start the senator
on I.V. Immunoglobulin, stat.

537
00:35:59.098 --> 00:36:01.831
Lfhe gets better, I'm right.
Lfhe dies, you're right.

538
00:36:40.666 --> 00:36:42.602
Dr. House?

539
00:36:48.150 --> 00:36:50.177
You faked that.
No.

540
00:36:51.325 --> 00:36:53.523
Say "antiretroviral."
Antiretroviral.

541
00:36:53.597 --> 00:36:56.502
Now, say it three times fast.

542
00:36:56.571 --> 00:36:59.236
We just got your latest blood results.
Your white cells are up.

543
00:36:59.311 --> 00:37:02.216
Your "T" cells
are back over a hundred.
That's-That's good, right?

544
00:37:02.285 --> 00:37:04.084
In a week? That's terrific.

545
00:37:04.156 --> 00:37:08.826
You'll need medication
for the rest of your life,
but other than that, you're fine.

546
00:37:08.901 --> 00:37:10.871
Am I well enough
to run for president?

547
00:37:10.939 --> 00:37:13.741
- Why not run for pope
while you're at it?
- Oh, come on.

548
00:37:13.813 --> 00:37:17.879
Kennedy had Addison's. F.D.R. Had polio.
Two of the best presidents
in the last hundred years.

549
00:37:17.956 --> 00:37:20.758
If they were running today,
they wouldn't stand a chance.
[Chuckling]

550
00:37:20.830 --> 00:37:23.928
You figure you'd be surgeon general
if you didn't have the limp?

551
00:37:25.173 --> 00:37:27.268
No. There's things I can't do.

552
00:37:27.345 --> 00:37:31.286
And like you said,
I... have to live with reality.

553
00:37:31.355 --> 00:37:33.622
Well, then I'm running.

554
00:37:33.694 --> 00:37:35.561
Good for you.

555
00:37:35.632 --> 00:37:39.334
Now, don't get excited.
He's right. I, uh- I won't win.

556
00:37:40.411 --> 00:37:42.974
Then why run?

557
00:37:44.521 --> 00:37:50.331
Oh, I see. Your point being,
the only way to make a difference
is to win every fight.

558
00:37:56.717 --> 00:37:58.710
But, hey, why listen to me?

559
00:37:58.788 --> 00:38:01.385
I own the company.
I'm certainly not to be trusted, right?

560
00:38:01.462 --> 00:38:03.956
[Laughter]

561
00:38:04.035 --> 00:38:07.133
Dr. Greg House,
on the other hand,
has a reputation...

562
00:38:07.209 --> 00:38:11.310
for integrity,
among other things.

563
00:38:11.385 --> 00:38:13.184
[Scattered Laughing]

564
00:38:13.257 --> 00:38:15.592
Ladies and gentlemen,
Dr. Greg House.

565
00:38:28.326 --> 00:38:30.797
[Electronic Feedback Hums]

566
00:38:33.306 --> 00:38:37.111
Eastbrook Pharmaceuticals'
extraordinary commitment
to research excellence...

567
00:38:37.182 --> 00:38:39.676
is exemplified
by their new ACE inhibitor,

568
00:38:39.755 --> 00:38:43.753
a breakthrough medical approach
that will protect millions
from heart disease.

569
00:38:54.524 --> 00:38:56.995
That's not a speech.

570
00:38:57.064 --> 00:38:59.433
I thought it was pithy.

571
00:38:59.502 --> 00:39:04.002
You got enough
for a press release anyhow.
Foreman or Cameron.

572
00:39:11.465 --> 00:39:13.458
[Chuckles]

573
00:39:14.806 --> 00:39:18.007
A few things I forgot to mention.

574
00:39:18.081 --> 00:39:21.316
Ed Vogler
is a brilliant businessman,

575
00:39:21.389 --> 00:39:23.792
a brilliant judge of people...

576
00:39:23.862 --> 00:39:27.769
and a man
who has never lost a fight.

577
00:39:29.409 --> 00:39:33.373
You know how I know
that the new ACE inhibitor is good?

578
00:39:33.452 --> 00:39:38.088
'Cause the old one was good.
The new one is really the same,
just more expensive.

579
00:39:39.166 --> 00:39:40.897
A lot more expensive.

580
00:39:40.970 --> 00:39:44.239
You see, that's another example
of Ed's brilliance.

581
00:39:44.311 --> 00:39:46.976
Whenever one ofhis drugs
is about to lose its patent,

582
00:39:47.051 --> 00:39:51.721
he has his boys and girls
alter itjust a tiny bit,
patent it all over again,

583
00:39:51.796 --> 00:39:54.792
making not just a pointless new pill,

584
00:39:54.870 --> 00:39:57.239
but millions and millions of dollars.

585
00:39:57.310 --> 00:39:59.907
Which is good for everybody, right?

586
00:39:59.982 --> 00:40:02.419
Except the patients.
But- [Scoffs] who cares?

587
00:40:02.489 --> 00:40:04.482
They're just so damn sick.

588
00:40:04.560 --> 00:40:06.929
God obviously
never liked them anyway.

589
00:40:08.570 --> 00:40:12.774
All the healthy people in the room,
let's have a big round of applause
for Ed Vogler.

590
00:40:12.847 --> 00:40:15.216
[House Applauding]

591
00:40:23.974 --> 00:40:25.807
I threw in a joke.

592
00:40:30.925 --> 00:40:33.419
~ [Piano]

593
00:40:48.601 --> 00:40:51.768
[Knocking]

594
00:41:20.244 --> 00:41:22.180
I'm sorry.

595
00:41:24.120 --> 00:41:27.457
I should've taken an extra couple
of Vicodin and just held my nose.

596
00:41:27.529 --> 00:41:31.630
- I'm guessing you did take
a couple extra Vicodin.
- True.

597
00:41:35.314 --> 00:41:39.552
You don't need to worry
about firing anyone.
I'm leaving.

598
00:41:41.228 --> 00:41:43.221
Why?

599
00:41:47.878 --> 00:41:51.614
Is this another noble,
self-sacrificing gesture?

600
00:41:52.757 --> 00:41:55.126
Are you trying
to protect Foreman?
No.

601
00:41:55.195 --> 00:41:58.066
So this is just,
"Don't fire me. I quit"?

602
00:41:58.136 --> 00:42:00.699
I'm protecting myself.

603
00:42:04.886 --> 00:42:07.984
You asked me why I like you.

604
00:42:09.063 --> 00:42:11.330
You're abrasive and rude.

605
00:42:12.971 --> 00:42:16.912
But I figured, everything you do,
you do it to help people.

606
00:42:19.087 --> 00:42:21.080
But I was wrong.

607
00:42:22.996 --> 00:42:24.989
You do it because it's right.

608
00:42:46.988 --> 00:42:50.223
There are only two ways
that I can deal with things.

609
00:42:51.231 --> 00:42:53.566
One is in my control.

610
00:42:57.413 --> 00:42:59.406
That's to leave.

611
00:43:05.500 --> 00:43:08.233
Good-bye, House.

612
00:44:06.380 --> 00:44:07.643
That's some bad hat, Harry.

9999
00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
